# Stage 0 - admission

Only for the NEW-task branch of "Always start here" in `SKILL.md` (`ppl recover --task
<TASK-ID>` came back `SCHEMA_INVALID`). If a run already existed, skip this stage entirely -
resume from the stage `ppl show` reported instead; calling `ppl init` on an existing run
raises `ILLEGAL_TRANSITION`.

1. `ppl init <TASK-ID> --tracker-url <url> --repo <worktree path> --harness <!-- include: harness/name -->` -
   `--repo` is the path the worktree will live at; Stage 1 creates it at exactly this path
   next, `ppl init` does not require it to exist yet. Leave `--isolated` at its default
   (true) unless the guard hook is registered somewhere broader than this launch directory -
   see `references/stage-8-after-merge.md` for what that flag controls. A run has to exist
   before the task is read, because a fetched issue is stored in the run.
2. <!-- include: tracker/admission -->
3. Check the admission list: one outcome, fixed governing revision (the one step 2 names), stable and verifiable
   acceptance criteria, closed material decisions, satisfied dependencies, risk tier, a
   non-empty write boundary, enumerated forbidden paths, a proof path defined before any
   implementation, and a budget.
4. Anything missing: `ppl escalate --code SPEC_GAP --question "..."` and stop. A task that
   fails admission does not get clarified along the way by a worker.
